  "rationale": [
    "Catalog packages have different inherent capabilities; a perfect shared twelve-answer knowledge, formatting and system-role test is not runtime availability.",
    "Each admission now needs two fresh unpredictable label checks: direct echo and multi-turn recall, executed through the original pinned template and exact native token IDs, with signed results from the same registered device.",
    "The expected label is generated per challenge and bound by the signed quote. Only the exact complete answer or enumerated presentation wrappers pass; arbitrary nonempty text does not.",
    "The original quality policies, failed runs and signed evidence remain preserved separately. Old failures never become readiness evidence; every model, including previously qualified Smart, performs fresh checks.",
    "Model hashes, tariff policy, reward weights, coverage, expiration, free-credit grants and financial ceilings remain unchanged. Availability rewards still count one actual capacity rather than every installed model."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Readiness is not broad answer quality, secure instruction hierarchy, or cryptographic loaded-weight attestation.",
    "The app observes a managed runtime and verifies the installed package/tokenizer; a malicious provider can spoof public software observations.",
    "Only updated workers advertising complete-inference checking may participate. Token-limit cutoffs, missing or stale answers, wrong devices and invalid signatures cannot pass.",
    "The existing model tariff permits at most 256 output tokens. A model that cannot complete these short checks within that bound and the 30-second deadline remains unavailable; no hardware-wide success is claimed.",
    "No credit purchases, reward transfers, free grants or fabricated model measurements are created by migration."
  ],
